n = 4 :  m = 3 tiles,  2^m = 8 tilings
==============================================================================
  sum of all stars = 0  (predicted 0, every tile has two endpoints): True
  rank(GAMMA) = 3   (predicted n-1 = 3): True
  quotient  F_2^m / GAMMA  has  2^(m-rank) = 1 cosets
  isomorphism classes : 4

  (Q1) is the coset b + GAMMA constant on each iso class?
       classes carrying MORE THAN ONE coset : 0 of 4
       -> the coset DESCENDS: it is a TOURNAMENT function.

  (Q2) cosets lying entirely inside a single iso class : 0 of 1
       -> the iso partition REFINES the coset partition (classes are
          unions of cosets): the coset is a COARSER tournament invariant.
  merged (complement-quotient) classes : 3
  quotient cosets : 1   -> equal to merged? False

  does a star move preserve the 3-cycle count c_3?  tilings where it does
     NOT : 8 of 8 sampled  -> c_3 is NOT a coset invariant

